&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Come join the organization that is redefining security for the AI era. As one of the&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wiz.io/blog/100m-arr-in-18-months-wiz-becomes-the-fastest-growing-software-company-ever&quot;&gt; fastest-growing startups ever,&lt;/a&gt; we enable teams to secure cloud and AI applications by connecting code, cloud, and runtime into a single shared context. Trusted by security teams all over the world, we have a proven&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.g2.com/products/wiz-wiz/reviews&quot;&gt; track record of success&lt;/a&gt; and a culture that values world-class talent. Not to mention, we&#39;re now&lt;a href=&quot;https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/identity-security/google-completes-acquisition-of-wiz&quot;&gt; powered by Google&lt;/a&gt;, meaning we offer our customers an AI-powered platform that harnesses Google’s Threat Intelligence and Security Operations to better detect, prevent, and respond to threats across all environments, allowing for further innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Wizards from all over the globe work together to protect the infrastructure of our customers, including over 65% of the Fortune 100, who trust us to scan and secure over 230 billion files daily. We’re honored to be a leading player in a massive and growing market, and we continue to look for exceptional Wizards who are eager to make a significant impact on our team. At Wiz, you’ll have the freedom to think creatively, dream big, and use your full range of skills to contribute to our momentous growth. Come join our team and help us create secure cloud environments that allow even the best companies to move faster, all while having some fun!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Regional Partner Marketing Programs Specialist, SEUR&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Spain (hybrid or remote: ideally around Madrid or Barcelona)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–3 years of experience in B2B or partner marketing or equivalent channel experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience executing marketing campaigns or partner engagement that drive pipeline and brand awareness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with platforms such as Looker, Salesforce, Notion, and Tableau.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Spanish &amp;amp; English.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in cloud, SaaS, or enterprise software industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational and project management skills with a high attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, collaborative mindset and a passion for strategic partner marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Strategic Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Align partner marketing programs to regional business priorities and sales goals for SEUR, and develop quarterly plans that reflect local market dynamics and partner ecosystem maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To-Partner Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive local partner communications, onboarding, and education initiatives, including newsletters, platform updates, enablement content, and portal engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;With-Partner Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Plan and execute joint marketing activities with priority partners (co-branded campaigns, regional events, webinars) and collaborate closely with Field Marketing to ensure integrated partner support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Through-Partner Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Localise and deliver scalable co-branded campaigns using global assets and frameworks, and work with global teams to adapt campaign toolkits for SEUR partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Tracking:&lt;/strong&gt; Track campaign ROI, pipeline contribution, and partner engagement metrics, maintaining reporting dashboards and providing actionable insights to optimise partner performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Integration Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Support onboarding and integration of new partners into marketing systems and workflows, coordinating with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Localized Partner Communications:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain a regional partner communications calendar, localising messaging to resonate with sales and technical audiences, and driving engagement within partner sales and technical communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wiz is seeking a Regional Partner Marketing Programs Specialist to own and execute our partner marketing strategy across the SEUR region. This is a high-impact, execution-focused role that supports strategic growth by activating partners through To-, With-, and Through-Partner marketing motions. The goal is to drive partner awareness, enablement, and pipeline aligned to local market dynamics, regional business priorities, and key strategic alliances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for a marketing professional with&lt;strong&gt; 2–3 years of B2B or partner marketing experience&lt;/strong&gt;, ideally in enterprise technology or SaaS. You will work closely with regional sales, global partner marketing, and field marketing teams to execute campaigns, scale enablement programs, and measure marketing performance across the partner ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;hands-on, execution-focused role&lt;/strong&gt; that offers a broad view across our EMEA partner ecosystem — covering Cloud Service Providers (CSP), Global System Integrators (GSI), resellers, and alliances — while providing exposure to both global programs and localised field execution to fuel growth.&lt;/p&gt;
