&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re looking for a talented &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Threat Research team under the CTO Office. In this role, you will be the engineering powerhouse of the research group, collaborating closely with security researchers to design and build cloud-native detection engines, automated platforms, and research infrastructure at massive scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build scalable, cloud-native detection engines and backend services to process security telemetry across massive cloud workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with security researchers to take raw attack concepts and POCs from ideation to production-ready systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and expand research platforms, testing frameworks, and automation pipelines that empower the team to test, validate, and deploy detection logic safely and rapidly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze, debug, and resolve problems across test, staging, and production environments, moving fast with a strong bias towards action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive engineering best practices, code quality, and security policies to ensure high reliability and performance at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customers in response to requests and questions when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
